{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/793816-how-much-separation-is-there-between-a-beast-and-their-horror","id":793816,"title":"How Much Separation Is There Between A Beast And Their Horror?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-27T15:42:44-08:00","id":793816,"title":"How Much Separation Is There Between A Beast And Their Horror?","content":"While it is not wrong to state that they are hybrid or gestalt entities, Beasts can still think in human terms, even if fear-focused, as shown by their Life trait that accompanies their Legend. Notably, Beasts who undergo any of the Inheritances lose their Life, IIRC. Would &quot;Find a way to become Incarnate but keep my humanity&quot; be a viable Aspiration, or is that metaphysically impossible?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T00:31:02-08:00","id":794661,"title":"","content":"I think that if you become a Beast Incarnate, you tie yourself to the Horror more closely, combining your Life and Legend into Myth. You don't so much lose your humanity as combine it into something else. Like, you don't lose a bar of metal if you make it into a sword, it's just in a different shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T08:40:06-08:00","id":794855,"title":"","content":"What the Beast loses is a human perspective on morality. In becoming Incarnate, the Beast accepts a worldview with himself at the center. Humans other supernaturals lose importance. The thing that matters is that the Incarnate feeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T07:08:12-08:00","id":797791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/793816-how-much-separation-is-there-between-a-beast-and-their-horror?p=794855#post794855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the Beast loses is a human perspective on morality. In becoming Incarnate, the Beast accepts a worldview with himself at the center. Humans other supernaturals lose importance. The thing that matters is that the Incarnate feeds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understood what you were saying up until this post, but recall that Beasts have no morality meter. I don't think the text argues that Beasts follow nor care for human ideals of morality in any capacity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T07:12:08-08:00","id":797794,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind there's at least an example of a character that preferred to commit suicide than to continue to torment the populace with his mere existence. So, I would take absolutes concerning individual character's morality or lack of thereof with a grain of salt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T07:18:26-08:00","id":797798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/793816-how-much-separation-is-there-between-a-beast-and-their-horror?p=797794#post797794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind there's at least an example of a character that preferred to commit suicide than to continue to torment the populace with his mere existence. So, I would take absolutes concerning individual character's morality or lack of thereof with a grain of salt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I definitely prefer the Integrity system in God Machine and 2e to the much too limiting and judgmental 1e system that assumed something was wrong with you if you drew a distinction between private and personal property. But let me just say, when I wrote my first draft of the Beast Dark Era, I specifically incorporated the Determining a Breaking Point rules for a semi-related mechanic I wanted to incorporate that I can't give specifics on. But it was removed entirely because Matt reminded me that Beasts do not use Integrity nor suffer Breaking Points. That is a direct albeit vague paraphrase of what I was told, I can't give specifics. Point is, I was specifically told when I tried to incorporate Breaking Points that Beasts do not suffer Breaking Points. My interpretation of that is that morality is scripted to be much more personal for Beasts than for others. I'm not sure how I personally feel about that being the case, but it's my textual claim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":".  Capitalization. 01-01-2016, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T09:24:39-08:00","id":797847,"title":"","content":"Like I've said here numerous times, Beasts behave like addicts, in that their worldview and behavior is colored by their Hungers, and that any moral stance that they take is incidental to whether they are indulging their Hunger or denying it. It's never just about right or wrong, but always about staying just hungry or full enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T11:07:00-08:00","id":797874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/793816-how-much-separation-is-there-between-a-beast-and-their-horror?p=797791#post797791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understood what you were saying up until this post, but recall that Beasts have no morality meter. I don't think the text argues that Beasts follow nor care for human ideals of morality in any capacity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What I meant with this was that a normal Beast doesn't have a human sense of morality, by and large, but becoming Incarnate completely scraps anything left. Beasts already have the perspective that 'that which feeds me is not wrong' , the Incarnate completely embraces this philosophy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T11:43:06-08:00","id":797896,"title":"","content":"Beast: the Primordial does have an Integrity-equivalent meter. Its called <i><b>Satiety</b></i>. It just so happens that Satiety also functions as a fuel stat in addition to its Integrity. The more sated you are, the more human-like you are. The lower your Satiety, the more of a monster you are. <br /> <br /> It should be noted that the higher your Lair, the harder you have at maintaining your Satiety, and thus your human urges. At any point you have low Integrity equivalent, you've got less human-like thoughts in you, even mundane mortals who go insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T13:03:24-08:00","id":797934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/793816-how-much-separation-is-there-between-a-beast-and-their-horror?p=797874#post797874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What I meant with this was that a normal Beast doesn't have a human sense of morality, by and large, but becoming Incarnate completely scraps anything left. Beasts already have the perspective that 'that which feeds me is not wrong' , the Incarnate completely embraces this philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for clarifying! I think I'm mostly in agreement.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/793816-how-much-separation-is-there-between-a-beast-and-their-horror?p=797896#post797896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast: the Primordial does have an Integrity-equivalent meter. Its called <i><b>Satiety</b></i>. It just so happens that Satiety also functions as a fuel stat in addition to its Integrity. The more sated you are, the more human-like you are. The lower your Satiety, the more of a monster you are.<br /> <br /> It should be noted that the higher your Lair, the harder you have at maintaining your Satiety, and thus your human urges. At any point you have low Integrity equivalent, you've got less human-like thoughts in you, even mundane mortals who go insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand what you're trying to say, but calling Satiety an Integrity-equivalent is disingenuous, in my opinion. Your Satiety is determined through an entirely different mechanism than Integrity or Humanity. I haven't read Idigam, so I can't comment there, but I would argue that it's different from all Morality meters in 1e. Yeah, starting Satiety can be as high as seven, but it starts at two. And it's determined largely by one's feeding habits, but it's also determined by the way your character interacts with her kin, Beasts and other critters alike. In a sense and in principle, that's similar maybe/kind-of to Synergy--it's probably the closest of the morality meters--but it's still different from even Synergy, more nuanced and a lot more fluctuating. If your issue is my direct statement that Beasts &quot;have no morality meter,&quot; with a lower-case 'm', I stand by that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":".  Last sentence. 01-01-2016, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T16:38:48-08:00","id":798018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/793816-how-much-separation-is-there-between-a-beast-and-their-horror?p=797934#post797934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand what you're trying to say, but calling Satiety an Integrity-equivalent is disingenuous, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not at all. I have a much larger post somehwere here where I go into huge analysis of the issue. Its not disingeuous. It might not obvious or something most people will realize at first blush, but that's because people are used to thinking of fuel and Integrity equivalents of being separate, when they're not here. Its a new twist for this game. <br /> <br /> Plus, I take a bit of issue with your word choice. I'm being completely sincere when I say this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your Satiety is determined through an entirely different mechanism than Integrity or Humanity. I haven't read Idigam, so I can't comment there, but I would argue that it's different from all Morality meters in 1e. </div> </div> </div> I suggest you read Werewolf then, because the Uratha have breaking poitns at both ends - going high and low over the course of the story without spending any exp is par for the course. Cover, for Demons, works completely differently as well. Humanity, for vampires, is the only one that's like Morality. Even Integrity itself doesn't work anything like Morality.<br /> <br /> Every game in 2e, so far, does their Integrity equivalent different. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, starting Satiety can be as high as seven, but it starts at two. And it's determined largely by one's feeding habits, but it's also determined by the way your character interacts with her kin, Beasts and other critters alike. </div> </div> </div> You mean, that if you have the connections to feed humanely through Family Dinner, and are careful and don't act monstrous, you'll start with Satiety 7? And having high Lair, acting more like a monster, and being careless indulging your Hunger leads you to Low Satiety? How is that not like high/low Integrity equivalents for everyone else?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If your issue is my direct statement that Beasts &quot;have no morality meter,&quot; with a lower-case 'm', I stand by that. </div> </div> </div>No game has &quot;morality meters&quot; anymore. Not even Vampire, which covers incidents like living too long, surviving something that should kill you, or joining a covenant. Integrity measures your Sanity, ala Call of Cthulhu; it doesn't drop when you commit sins, it drops when you're exposed to mind breaking horrors. Harmony is balacning Flesh and Spirit. Cover is how well you dodge notice. Wisdom is possibly the closest, which covers misuse of magic, and we haven't seen its final form yet, so that's debatable. Morals are too dependant upon where and how you grew up - trying to make one into a mechanic is doomed to failure. <br /> <br /> The assumption that Beasts don't follow any form of human morality because of a lack of Integrity equivalent is grossly flawed. No game measures morality, and yet many of the supernaturals do have human morals. They were raised as humans for a long time, after all, and they don't just suddenly lose their upbringing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T17:14:47-08:00","id":798029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/793816-how-much-separation-is-there-between-a-beast-and-their-horror?p=798018#post798018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not at all. I have a much larger post somehwere here where I go into huge analysis of the issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you link to this? Perspective might help this discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T18:11:24-08:00","id":798046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/793816-how-much-separation-is-there-between-a-beast-and-their-horror?p=798029#post798029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you link to this? Perspective might help this discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div> I believe MCN is referring to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/643006-an-analysis-on-satiety-and-feeding-hungers\"><b>this thread</b></a>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}